{"id": "ask-person-draft-first", "area": "surface", "kind": "bad", "source": {"commit": "8b9e12b86a95fe4db98b2389d49102f237b4b7bc", "note": "Sanitized from a real ask: the draft sat under task IDs, timestamps and unrelated history, and the card's fold hid it."}, "profile": "task", "turns": ["Raised by the memory light pass on Nov 19 at about 21:05Z. Your prospect Dana Reyes (Chief Information Officer, Example Health, CRM record) accepted your LinkedIn connection request at about 19:13Z today. The prospecting task (thr_00000000-0000-4000-8000-0000000000a1, \"Find enterprise prospects\") posted a DM draft for her in message msg_00000000-0000-4000-8000-0000000000b2 at 19:13:54Z. You have not answered it. You approved a different DM, Sam Lee's, at 20:20Z, and Sam's DM was sent at 20:22Z. Dana's draft is not sent.\n\nThe draft, exactly as posted:\n\nHi Dana, I'm building Example to deploy secure AI agents for enterprises. We're building a shared knowledge base that employees' agents can update and use in real time, with controls over what each agent can access.\n\nI'd love to learn about your biggest pain points in deploying AI agents across your organization. Would you be open to a quick chat?\n\nDo this:\n1. Earlier research could not confirm whether you already messaged Dana. Say so in the question.\n2. Ask with ask_person: \"Send this DM to Dana Reyes (Example Health)?\" Include the full draft text, unchanged. Offer Yes, No and Edit.\n3. Send nothing yet. After asking, end this turn."], "mocks": {"ask_person": {"kind": "person.question", "replayed": false, "requestId": "req_00000000-0000-4000-8000-0000000000c3", "status": "pending", "next": "Your question is waiting in Needs you. End this turn; the answer continues this task."}}, "expect": {"calls": [{"tool": "ask_person", "args": {}}], "callsArgMatch": [{"tool": "ask_person", "path": ["detail"], "pattern": "^```draft\\nHi Dana, I'm building Example to deploy secure AI agents for enterprises\\. We're building a shared knowledge base that employees' agents can update and use in real time, with controls over what each agent can access\\.\\n\\nI'd love to learn about your biggest pain points in deploying AI agents across your organization\\. Would you be open to a quick chat\\?\\n```[ \\t]*(?:\\n|$)", "first": true, "args": {}}], "notCallsArgMatch": [{"tool": "ask_person", "path": ["detail"], "pattern": "thr_|msg_|\\d{1,2}:\\d{2}(:\\d{2})?Z|Sam", "args": {}}]}}
{"id": "ask-person-choice-without-draft", "area": "surface", "kind": "guard", "source": {"commit": "8b9e12b86a95fe4db98b2389d49102f237b4b7bc", "note": "A draft fence is for words the person would send; a plain choice gets none."}, "profile": "task", "turns": ["Our team offsite can be Tuesday at the lake house or Thursday at the city office; both are free and cost the same. Ask me which one with ask_person, then end the turn."], "mocks": {"ask_person": {"kind": "person.question", "replayed": false, "requestId": "req_00000000-0000-4000-8000-0000000000c3", "status": "pending", "next": "Your question is waiting in Needs you. End this turn; the answer continues this task."}}, "expect": {"calls": [{"tool": "ask_person", "args": {}}], "notCallsArgMatch": [{"tool": "ask_person", "path": ["detail"], "pattern": "```", "args": {}}]}}
